            "review_title": "Review at ChinChin Bar",
            "review_text": "Steve H\n2 contributions\n0\nBe very careful with the staff!\nSep 2024 • Friends\nChiChin is the only upscale gay bar in Saigon’s District 1. The interior is very nice, offering an elevated experience with air conditioning. It’s usually quiet on weekdays but gets super packed on weekends, especially on Fridays (fun drag show around 11 PM) and Saturdays (busiest night).\n\nWhen it’s slow, the staff is perfect. However, when it gets busy, be cautious. They might short-change you or “forget” to bring drinks you’ve paid for. We reserved a table for Saturday, and while I was putting my cash away, the AC was blasted (which felt good and helped with the smoke, as they allow smoking, including cigars). My cash fell onto the floor, and a waiter quickly picked it up, asking if it was mine. He then ran off with all my cash, claiming it was his. I had to go to the manager, and after some arguing, I offered 200,000 VND to get my cash back.\n\nOverall, you must watch the wait staff as they can’t be trusted. The “forgotten” drinks happened three times. It’s sad because everything else about the bar is excellent. Be very careful with the staff!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten September 16, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
