            "review_title": "Review at ChinChin Bar",
            "review_text": "Trevor K\n63 contributions\n1\nCozy bar marred by awful music\nAug 2022\nChinChin is quaint, cozy, has good drinks and plays some of the most inappropriate bar music. \n\nI get it, taste in music is completely subjective, but going into an empty bar at 7pm on a Monday (and Wednesday) and hearing rap / hip-hop blasting on the speakers is nothing short of jarring.\n\nWho on earth wants to pay nearly 200,000 VND for a drink and listen to words like n*gg*r, f*ck and c*nt over and over? Music in a bar or restaurant is supposed to compliment the space, not detract from it. \n\nI don’t know who this bar is trying to attract (certainly no one on the two nights I was there). \n\nChinChin’s social media pages seem to imply the bar has “gay leanings,” but I’ve never visited a gay bar in any country that plays music that is noted for its rampant homophobia and misogyny. \n\nI doubt I’ll come here again, but if I did it would only be late at night when (hopefully) the sound of chatter would drown out the so-called “music.”\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 4, 2022",
